1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,129
This is LifecycleKASE, a corporate action terminal for tokenized bonds.

2
00:00:05,129 --> 00:00:09,857
We are using the running application in English, through walletless QA.

3
00:00:09,857 --> 00:00:15,351
These interactions simulate all payments, approvals, and burns inside this page.

4
00:00:15,351 --> 00:00:21,039
The instrument registry exposes terms, circulating supply, and lifecycle status.

5
00:00:21,039 --> 00:00:25,458
Investor records connect identity, eligibility, and wallets.

6
00:00:25,458 --> 00:00:32,636
We will demonstrate coupon, partial early redemption, and redemption at maturity on synthetic test records.

7
00:00:32,636 --> 00:00:36,985
We schedule the coupon, capture holders, and calculate rights.

8
00:00:36,985 --> 00:00:44,453
The QA positions are ten, twenty, and five bonds; entitlements total seventeen hundred fifty KZT-Test.

9
00:00:44,453 --> 00:00:47,687
The issuer funds and reserves the full budget.

10
00:00:47,687 --> 00:00:54,835
A distinct approver reviews the calculation, then the issuer pays each holder and finalizes the simulated receipt.

11
00:00:54,835 --> 00:00:58,779
Next, we open twenty percent partial redemption.

12
00:00:58,779 --> 00:01:05,342
Capture and calculation produce seven bonds to redeem, with seven thousand KZT-Test in payment.

13
00:01:05,342 --> 00:01:09,731
Again, full reserve and separate approval precede execution.

14
00:01:09,731 --> 00:01:15,640
After the three simulated payments and burns, supply changes from thirty five to twenty eight.

15
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:21,448
In the Solana protocol, each holder payment and burn share one atomic transaction.

16
00:01:21,448 --> 00:01:26,092
Maturity captures the remaining twenty eight bonds in this QA sequence.

17
00:01:26,092 --> 00:01:31,840
Principal plus the final coupon totals twenty nine thousand four hundred KZT-Test.

18
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:38,033
We reserve funds, switch approver, execute the simulated payments, and finalize.

19
00:01:38,033 --> 00:01:44,277
All remaining bonds are burned, final supply is zero, and the instrument becomes redeemed.

20
00:01:44,277 --> 00:01:49,435
We download the simulated result and inspect transaction and audit history as an auditor.

21
00:01:49,435 --> 00:01:53,429
QA receipts do not establish blockchain execution.

22
00:01:53,429 --> 00:02:01,757
The production recovery path preserves an unknown operation and its original signature for verification, instead of sending a replacement payment.

23
00:02:01,757 --> 00:02:07,335
Separate October twelfth disposable Localnet acceptance completed these four actions.

24
00:02:07,335 --> 00:02:12,734
It includes an additional exact eight unit redemption between percentage redemption and maturity.

25
00:02:12,734 --> 00:02:19,397
That is why its maturity pays twenty one thousand and burns twenty, rather than the QA sequence of twenty eight.

26
00:02:19,397 --> 00:02:24,171
Canonical receipts reconcile finalized cash and token effects.

27
00:02:24,171 --> 00:02:28,200
KZT-Test and investor eligibility are simulated.

28
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:32,903
The repository contains original receipts and reproduction instructions.

29
00:02:32,903 --> 00:02:40,461
Real KYC, fiat settlement, public-network acceptance, and exchange integration remain future work.

30
00:02:40,461 --> 00:02:44,815
LifecycleKASE is not affiliated with or approved by KASE.
